WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:04.080
Speaker 1: And finally today,&nbsp;
speaking of serious trouble,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:12.180
how do you feel about going to war in Mexico?&nbsp;
Not war with Mexico, folks. But Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:19.980
are warming up to the idea of using the&nbsp;
United States military to take on those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:27.180
nasty drug cartels down in Mexico. Let me&nbsp;
read you this from Politico. In recent weeks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:33.540
Donald Trump has discussed sending special forces&nbsp;
and using cyber warfare to target cartel leaders.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:39.180
If he's reelected president and Per Rolling Stone&nbsp;
asked for, quote, battle plans to strike Mexico.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:45.240
Representatives Dan Crenshaw and Mike Waltz,&nbsp;
both Republicans, introduced a bill seeking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:51.720
authorization for the use of military force to&nbsp;
put us at war with the cartels. Senator Tom Cart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:57.300
Tom Cotton of Arkansas, said he is open to sending&nbsp;
U.S. troops into Mexico to target drug lords, even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:03.060
without that nation's permission. And lawmakers&nbsp;
in both chambers have filed legislation to label&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:09.540
some cartels as foreign terrorist organizations,&nbsp;
a move supported by GOP presidential aspirants.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:18.480
So labeling drug cartels as terrorist&nbsp;
organizations basically gives the government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:25.260
a lot more leeway to send in U.S. troops without,&nbsp;
of course, having to go through getting all that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:31.380
authorization from Congress officially declaring&nbsp;
war. If we can just slap a broad label on them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:36.900
we can kind of kill whoever we want to kill.&nbsp;
And that is unfortunately, the way that our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:43.680
government is set up in a post-9-11 world. Here's&nbsp;
the thing. This really isn't about the drugs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.760
It's not. Believe it or not, it's not&nbsp;
about the drugs. What this is about.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:57.240
Is being able to bomb a sovereign nation, to&nbsp;
shoot whoever we want to shoot down in Mexico&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:06.120
by claiming they're a drug smuggler. Now imagine,&nbsp;
if you will, a caravan, let's call it a caravan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:12.780
of people approaching our southern border.&nbsp;
And then folks on Fox News and Republican&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:17.340
politicians and candidates tell us we know a&nbsp;
lot of these people are are smuggling drugs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:25.980
Suddenly. You're able to apply that&nbsp;
terrorist label to these so-called caravans.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:31.560
And you can send one missile. You send&nbsp;
a drone down there to take them out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:39.240
That's what this is about. It's not about&nbsp;
the drugs, folks. It is not about the drugs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:45.180
It is about getting that label so&nbsp;
that they can use the military force,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:50.700
so that they can attack migrants, so that they&nbsp;
can attack asylum seekers all by claiming,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:53.220
nope, they had drugs, they were&nbsp;
smuggling drugs. We'll never know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.980
right? I mean, we'll never be able to fully&nbsp;
find out if they did or didn't have drugs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:06.840
And that's the plan. That's what this is&nbsp;
about. This is about a show of force on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:12.840
our southern border, not deep in Mexico, but on&nbsp;
our southern border, giving the United States,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:19.560
the Republican Party the ability to kill anybody&nbsp;
that they don't want in this country. That's all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:24.720
the time we have for today. But we've got a great&nbsp;
bonus show coming up for you. I am Farron Cousins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:29.160
from Ring of Fire. Thank you so much for&nbsp;
watching today. I'll see you again tomorrow.

